lback). Note: payments-api v5.1.0 also shows as degraded with an 18% error rate. A rollback of payments-api to v5.0.0 was proposed, but the approver denied it and said the root cause is in payments-worker. Check whether payments-api recovers now that payments-worker is rolled back.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll check whether payments-api recovered after the worker rollback.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012TfYQzgirswCS9HQNnsEPJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 in all regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call. payments-worker is healthy again, but payments-api is still failing.\n\n**How I found the right service:** there's no service called just \"payments\". I found payments-api first: it was unhealthy on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate, so I tried to roll it back to v5.0.0. The approver denied that and said the problem is in payments-worker.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. **Rolled back payments-worker:** v3.4.0 was unhealthy in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. I rolled it back to v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production. The approver approved this. It's now healthy, with a 0.2% error rate.\n2. **Opened INC-0001 (SEV2) for payments-worker:** the summary covers the rollback and notes the payments-api problem.\n\n**Still broken:** payments-api is still unhealthy after the worker rollback. It's on v5.1.0 in all regions with an 18% error rate. Its last healthy release is v5.0.0. I haven't touched it because the approver blocked that rollback. Someone needs to decide whether to investigate it separately or ask again for approval to roll it back to v5.0.0.", "type": "text"}]}]}